pend `blocked [at=<epoch>]: {why}` and stop; firstmate will help.\0126. If a decision belongs above the implementation worker (product choices, destructive actions),\012   append `needs-decision [at=<epoch>]: {summary of options}` and stop. Firstmate will reply with the decision.\012   For a no-mistakes ask-user gate specifically, escalate all ask-user findings as one event plus one snapshot file, using that same shape even when the gate holds only a single ask-user finding: write only the ask-user findings, verbatim and unparaphrased (id, severity, file, line, description, authority), to `/Users/eduardopicazo/orca/workspaces/firstmate/casco-mate/data/391-sleepfor-listener/nm-<run>-findings.txt`, then report the gate with\012   `needs-decision [at=<epoch>] [key=nm-<run>-<step>]: ask-user findings=<id1>,<id2>,... file=/Users/eduardopicazo/orca/workspaces/firstmate/casco-mate/data/391-sleepfor-listener/nm-<run>-findings.txt`\012   naming every ask-user finding id from that gate. The status line only points at the file; it never restates or summarizes a finding's content.\012   A decision or blocker you opened stays open until a `resolved` line carrying its exact key lands; a later `done:` or `working:` line never closes it, even when the answer is what started that work.\012   Firstmate's reply normally writes that closing line at answer time; when a blocker or wait clears WITHOUT a firstmate reply, append `resolved [at=<epoch>]: {how it cleared}` yourself (same `[key=<slug>]` if you opened it with one) as you resume.\0127. Never administer infrastructure that every lane shares. Two things are shared:\012   - The `no-mistakes` daemon - one instance serving every lane/home, so stopping, restarting, or\012     updating it kills other lanes' in-flight pipeline runs; only firstmate manages the daemon.\012     Before you append `blocked:` about the pipeline, run `no-mistakes daemon status` and\012     `no-mistakes axi status`. If the daemon socket refuses connections or is