leness beyond confirming whether it shares this cause (note it in the PR if not), and any unrelated watcher refactor.\012\012# Herdr lifecycle declaration - NOT ENABLED\012**HARD SAFETY GATE:** this scaffold cannot inspect the task text filled in above.\012If the task will start, stop, delete, restart, profile, or otherwise drive Herdr lifecycle behavior, stop and regenerate the brief with `--herdr-lab` before dispatch.\012Do not add Herdr lifecycle commands to this unguarded brief by hand.\012\012# Setup\012You are in a disposable git worktree of firstmate-fork, at a detached HEAD on a clean default branch.\012\012**Verify isolation before anything else.** Run `pwd -P` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; both must resolve to the disposable task worktree you were launched in, such as a treehouse pool path or an Orca-managed worktree, not the primary checkout firstmate operates from.\012The path check is authoritative: `git rev-parse --git-dir` and `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` can help inspect the repo, but they do not prove you are outside the primary checkout.\012If the top-level path is the primary checkout or not the worktree you were launched in, STOP - do not branch or commit here - append `blocked [at=<epoch>]: launched in primary checkout, not an isolated worktree` to the status file and stop.\012\0121. First action: create your branch: `git checkout -b fm/fm-sm-watch-herdr-env --`\0122. Run `no-mistakes doctor`; if it reports the repo is not initialized here, run `no-mistakes init`.\012\012# Rules\0121. Never push to the default branch. Never merge a PR.\0122. Keep project edits inside this worktree; keep proof and scratch output outside it, under `/Users/eduardopicazo/orca/projects/firstmate/data/fm-sm-watch-herdr-env/` or a temporary directory.\012   Outside the worktree, write only that task material and the status and steering-inbox records authorized below.\012   Leave the worktree clean before reporting done.\0123. Use gh-axi for GitHub operations